-- title:
--   Congruent mathbf Z_{(ℓ)}-points of an odd-order Hopf ℤ-model agree
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be primes with $q \neq 2$, and let $K$ be a commutative ring carrying the structure of a Hopf algebra over $\mathbf Z$ which is of finite type as a $\mathbf Z$-algebra and flat as a $\mathbf Z$-module. Write $\mathbf Z_{(\ell)}$ for the subring of $\mathbf Q$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. Assume: for every prime $\ell \neq p$ the tensor product $\mathbf Z_{(\ell)} \otimes_{\mathbf Z} K$ is a finite $\mathbf Z_{(\ell)}$-module; the number of $\mathbf Z$-algebra homomorphisms $K \to \overline{\mathbf Q}$ is exactly $q$; and every ring automorphism $\sigma$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ satisfies $\sigma(\psi(k)) = \psi(k)$ for every $\mathbf Z$-algebra homomorphism $\psi \colon K \to \overline{\mathbf Q}$ and every $k \in K$. Let $\ell$ be a prime (not required to differ from $p$ or $q$) and let $\chi, \chi' \colon K \to \mathbf Z_{(\ell)}$ be ring homomorphisms such that $\chi(k) - \chi'(k)$ lies in the ideal of $\mathbf Z_{(\ell)}$ generated by $\ell$ for every $k \in K$. Then $\chi = \chi'$.
--
--   Geometrically this says that for a flat finite-type Hopf $\mathbf Z$-model $\operatorname{Spec} K$ of the constant group scheme of odd prime order $q$ with everywhere-rational, Galois-invariant geometric points, the reduction map from $\mathbf Z_{(\ell)}$-points to points mod $\ell$ is injective; classically this reflects the étaleness of finite flat group schemes of order invertible on the base together with the Tate–Oort and Raynaud uniqueness of finite flat models of $\mathbf Z/q$ in small ramification. It feeds the construction of a complete family of orthogonal idempotents exhibiting $K$ as the group algebra of $\mathbf Z/q$, used in the analysis of prime-order group schemes over $\mathbf Z$ in the level-lowering part of the argument.
